          "description": "Monitoring target is where Private Traffic Manager will gather health information.It can differ from the endpoint target, for example when the target is an IPv6 address. If not configured, the endpoint target is used. It is required when the target is IPv6 and cannot itself be an IPv6 address.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "priority": {
          "description": "The priority of this endpoint when using the 'Priority' traffic routing method. Possible values are from 1 to 1000, lower values represent higher priority. This is an optional parameter.  If specified, it must be specified on all endpoints, and no two endpoints can share the same priority value.",
